Z||000000||GeeDee86GT||11-21-2000||12:21 PM||||I can't roll my parts car. it was pushed at the wreckers, has no clutch slave cyl, and has wheel locks (no key). The drive axle is locked solid. Can I free it so it can be pushed?? or should I make a dolly for it? <P>Thx, Gary<BR>86SE, '84 parts car, '84 sledgehammer bait!||||reg||8
Z||000001||Tigger||11-21-2000||12:47 PM||||I think you can get a wheel lock remover kit at an auto parts store, they aren't cheap, but once you have the kit, you've always got it.  Check into that, another alternative would be to weld a junk socket to the lug and turn them off.<P>Is the tranny in neutral?  Not sure what I'd do if the tranny won't go out of gear.  Probably make a dolly or pull the halfshafts.  If it's not that then chances are the calipers are stuck or the e-brake is hung up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||11-22-2000||02:02 AM||||if you are not able to put the tranny in neutral by the gearshift, disconnect the cable(s) on the tranny and move the gear selector by hand. If the calipers are frosen you may have to remove them to move the car. If it is the e-brake, remove the springs on each caliper and remove the ends of the e-brake cables from the perch (same as the springs connect to.<P>As for the wheel locks, weld a second lug nut to the one with the lock and remove it, or pound a socket over it, or, buy the wheel lock kit - I know NAPA carries them and they are around $50||||reg||1
